WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:04.280
When it comes to landing Hollywood's most
coveted roles, even established actors have

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:05.480
to show a little hustle.

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:09.080
With the knowledge that Ben Affleck will no
longer be reprising his role as the Caped

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:14.400
Crusader for director Matt Reeves' The Batman,
an actor from DC's Man of Steel has tossed

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.960
his name into the running for the gig.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:20.520
While the next standalone Batman movie was
originally set to be written by, directed

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:25.520
by, and star Ben Affleck, the two-time Batman
actor has instead stepped back, leaving the

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:26.660
role wide open.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:31.550
Since then, fans have been buzzing about which
stars might step up and don the cape and cowl

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:32.870
in Affleck's stead.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:37.400
The most recent name to pop up in association
with The Batman has been Robert Pattinson,

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:42.120
the British actor who broke into the mainstream
as the glittery vampire Edward Cullen in the

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:43.700
Twilight film franchise.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:48.540
Though Pattinson has since gone on to prove
himself as a capable dramatic actor with movies

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:53.020
like Good Time and Maps to the Stars, the
internet still reacted somewhat poorly to

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:55.180
rumors of his involvement in The Batman.

00:00:55.460 --> 00:01:00.180
The backlash gave other actors plenty of opportunities
to throw their own hats into the ring.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:04.780
One voice in the anti-Pattinson-as-Batman
camp offered their own alternative thoughts

00:01:04.789 --> 00:01:09.249
about who should play the lead in Reeves'
upcoming feature, instead pointing to Christopher

00:01:09.249 --> 00:01:13.640
Meloni, who appeared as Colonel Nathan Hardy
in 2013's Man of Steel.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.220
"This man is not our enemy."

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.719
"Thank you, Colonel."

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:25.659
Writing on Twitter in early February, user
Emily Diaz made an emphatic case for the longtime

00:01:25.659 --> 00:01:29.929
character actor, writing, "NO, NO, and a million
times NO, dude!

00:01:29.929 --> 00:01:32.539
Robert Pattinson would make a terrible Batman.

00:01:32.539 --> 00:01:36.029
I think Chris Meloni would make an excellent
Batman-slash-Bruce Wayne."

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:41.020
Meloni, who is most recognizable from his
lead role as NYPD Detective Elliot Stabler

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:45.409
on Law &amp; Order: Special Victims Unit, quickly
caught wind of the fan's desire to see him

00:01:45.409 --> 00:01:47.760
grab the superhero torch from Affleck.

00:01:48.009 --> 00:01:51.800
The actor took to his own Twitter page to
retweet the post, revealing that he would

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:53.400
indeed love to play the Batman.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:58.140
As Meloni wrote in his post, "Yo DC Comics,
this is what the kids call, 'going VIRAL!'

00:01:58.340 --> 00:01:59.340
Pull the trigger.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:00.020
I'm ready.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:00.520
I'm…

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:01.260
BATMAN."

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:05.760
Meloni as the Caped Crusader is a fun thing
to think about, and the actor is no stranger

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.140
to the world of comic books.

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:11.820
On top of his role in Man of Steel, the actor
has also appeared in the comic book adaptation

00:02:11.829 --> 00:02:17.170
Sin City: A Dame to Kill For, based on the
comic series by Frank Miller, as well as the

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:21.500
SYFY TV series Happy, based on a mini-series
by Grant Morrison.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:26.560
Meloni's enthusiasm is also a refreshing change
of pace from the last few years of Bat-Fleck,

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:31.540
which saw the Argo director seeming to become
less and less enthusiastic about the role.

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:36.480
Now that Affleck is moving out of Gotham City,
plenty of new actors' names have emerged for

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:41.760
consideration, including English actor Jack
O'Connell, Stranger Things star Dacre Montgomery,

00:02:41.769 --> 00:02:44.040
and singer-songwriter Nick Jonas.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:48.189
When Reeves first signed on to direct The
Batman, it was briefly rumored that the Dawn

00:02:48.189 --> 00:02:52.510
of the Planet of the Apes director wanted
Jake Gyllenhaal in the lead role, a possibility

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:54.760
that Gyllenhaal himself later shot down.

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:59.280
Gyllenhaal instead signed on with Marvel Studios
to play the villain in Spider-Man: Far From

00:02:59.280 --> 00:02:59.780
Home.

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:04.380
Another actor who's been rumored to be angling
for the role is Mad Men star Jon Hamm, who

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:06.980
was once said to be "gunning hard" for the
gig.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:11.500
However, it seems unlikely that either he
or Meloni will ultimately get the part.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:16.320
Unfortunately, despite Meloni's enthusiasm,
it doesn't seem likely that Reeves and company

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:18.220
will end up selecting him for the role.

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:24.020
One limiting factor is Meloni's age, with
his 57 years falling far outside the late-20s-to-early-30s

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:27.550
range that Warner Bros. seems to be looking
for.

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:31.590
It's been reported that Reeves' take on The
Batman will focus on a younger version of

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:36.359
the caped crusader, which stands in contrast
to Affleck's version of an older, grizzled,

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:37.840
more world-weary character.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:41.800
Meloni may be a versatile actor, but a young
man he is not.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:46.620
Despite all that, history tells us that nothing
is set in stone when it comes to The Batman,

00:03:46.629 --> 00:03:50.930
so if the producers of the movie decide on
a radically different approach, Meloni is

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.959
waiting in the wings to take the job.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:56.660
And if he doesn't get the lead role, who knows,
he might still end up in the movie.

00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:01.120
Donald Glover's campaign to play Spider-Man
didn't get him cast as the webslinger, but

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:03.200
he did still end up in Spider-Man: Homecoming.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:07.620
Maybe Meloni could get cast as a villain,
and put his intensity to good use against

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:09.790
whoever ends up actually donning the cowl.

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:14.580
We'll find out what happens when The Batman
hits theaters on June 25th, 2021.

